<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">14 December in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 14 December, from 557 to 1911.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/constantinople.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">557 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,469 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">An earthquake shakes Constantinople and weakens Hagia Sophia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A powerful earthquake damaged much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> and cracked the great dome of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hagia-sophia">Hagia Sophia</a>, which collapsed the following May. It was rebuilt higher and rededicated in 562.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hagia-sophia">Hagia Sophia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1503">1503 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">523 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nostradamus is born in Saint-Rémy-de-Provence</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Michel de Nostredame, physician and astrologer, was born in Provence. His Prophecies of 1555, written in vague rhymed quatrains, have been claimed as predictions of countless later events.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1799">1799 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">227 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">George Washington dies at Mount Vernon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-washington">George Washington</a> died aged 67 after a throat infection, worsened by heavy bloodletting. Having twice given up power, as commander and as president, he was mourned as the father of his country.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1900">1900 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">126 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Max Planck presents the quantum hypothesis</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Before the German Physical Society in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a>, Max Planck proposed that energy is emitted in discrete packets, or quanta. The idea, introduced to solve a problem in heat radiation, became the basis of quantum physics.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1911">1911 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">115 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Roald Amundsen's party reaches the South Pole</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Norwegian explorer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roald-amundsen">Roald Amundsen</a> and four companions became the first people to reach the South Pole. Robert Falcon Scott's British party arrived 34 days later to find the Norwegian tent and flag.</p></div></li></ol>
